{
  "workflowId": "300000331058562",
  "workflowCode": "ORA_GTM_PRODUCT_CLASSIFICATION_ASSISTANT",
  "name": "GTM Product Classification Assistant",
  "description": "Assists with product classification for global trade compliance. Using LLMs, this assistant generates proposed HS codes and descriptions from product specifications, BOMs, and regulatory documents. It assists with compliance with global trade regulations by integrating relevant regulatory information.",
  "specification": {
    "jsonSchemaName": "Workflow.spec",
    "jsonSchemaVersion": "1",
    "inputs": [],
    "outputSpecification": " ",
    "agentsValueMappings": [],
    "dataPipeline": {
      "pipelineNodes": [
        {
          "metadata": {
            "description": "Start of data pipeline",
            "name": "Start"
          },
          "outcomes": {
            "success": "1764695239219"
          },
          "code": "START",
          "id": "start",
          "inputs": [],
          "type": "START"
        },
        {
          "metadata": {
            "description": "End of data pipeline",
            "name": "End"
          },
          "outcomes": {},
          "code": "END",
          "id": "end",
          "inputs": [],
          "type": "END"
        },
        {
          "metadata": {
            "name": "Parse Input Message"
          },
          "outcomes": {
            "success": "1766386564104"
          },
          "code": "OTM_PCA_INPUT",
          "id": "1764695239219",
          "inputs": [
            {
              "id": "1764695239223_1",
              "name": "prompt",
              "type": "string",
              "value": "From the user input text - {{$context.$system.$inputMessage}}, perform the following tasks:\n\n1. Identify the Item :\n           1.0 Detection guidance (important):\n                  - The item name is a product identifier, not a natural language phrase and is alphanumeric.\n           1.1 Item name is of the format <domain>.<item_xid>. item_xid can contain special characters and spaces. There can be cases where domain is missing . In that case, item name is same as item_xid.\n           1.2  Extract the item name from the user input text.\n           1.3 Convert item name to uppercase.\n           1.4 Assign the result to property itemGidWithoutEncoding.\n           1.5 URL encode the result and assign it to the property itemGid.\n           1.6 If item name is not present in the input, leave itemGid as an empty string: \"\".\n2. Product Classification Type:\n           2.1 Locate the product classification type in the user input text. Possible values include: \"HTS US\", \"ECCN US\", \"HTS MX\", or \"SCHEDULE B\". This is not an exhaustive list. Look for similar data.\n           2.2 If not present in the input, leave the product classification type as empty string :\"\".\n           2.3 Convert the extracted value to uppercase. Assign the extracted value to the property prodClassType.\n3. Country of Import:\n            3.1 Determine the country associated with the product classification type:\n                   3.1.1 Example : For \"HTS US\", \"ECCN US\", and \"SCHEDULE B\" use \"US\". For \"HTS MX\" use \"Mexico\".                   \n            3.2 If neither product classification type nor country is present, leave both as empty string :\"\".\n            3.4 Assign this country to the property countryOfImport.\n4. Confidence of prediction threshold:\n            4.1 Extract the confidence from the user input text.\n                   4.1.1 Remove % symbol if present. The value of confidence should be between 0 to 100.\n                   4.1.2 If confidence is not present, default the value to 95.\n            4.2 Assign this confidence to the property confidenceThreshold.\n5. Remark qualifiers:\n            5.1 Identify remark qualifiers (or remarks) from the user input text.\n            5.2 Add each remark qualifier to array property remarkQualifiers.\n            5.3 If remark qualifiers are not present in the text, keep the array empty.\n            5.4 remarkQualifiers property should be a valid JSON array."
            }
          ],
          "outputSpecification": "{\n    \"$schema\": \"http://json-schema.org/draft-04/schema#\",\n    \"type\": \"object\",\n    \"properties\": {\n        \"itemGidWithoutEncoding\": {\n            \"type\": \"string\"\n        },\n        \"remarkQualifiers\": {\n            \"type\": \"array\",\n            \"items\": {\n                \"type\": \"object\",\n                \"properties\": {}\n            }\n        },\n        \"confidenceThreshold\": {\n            \"type\": \"number\"\n        },\n        \"countryOfImport\": {\n            \"type\": \"string\"\n        },\n        \"prodClassType\": {\n            \"type\": \"string\"\n        },\n        \"itemGid\": {\n            \"type\": \"string\"\n        }\n    }\n}",
          "type": "LLM"
        },
        {
          "metadata": {
            "name": "Format output"
          },
          "outcomes": {
            "success": "1766994258161"
          },
          "code": "FORMAT_OUTPUT",
          "convergenceTargetId": "1766038330154",
          "id": "1765963748879",
          "inputs": [
            {
              "id": "1765963748883_1",
              "name": "prompt",
              "type": "string",
              "value": "Format the output of {{$context.$nodes.CUSTOMS_DESCRIPTION_GENERATOR.$output}} + {{$context.$nodes.TARIFF_DETAILS_GENERATOR.$output}} as given in Sample output below in a structured format. \n\nSample output format: NOTE- THIS IS ONLY AN EXAMPLE. DO NOT DISPLAY THIS DATA IN THE OUTPUT. ONLY USE THIS TO FORMAT THE OUTPUT.\n\n PRODUCT CLASSIFICATION ASSISTANT\n\nProduct: Stainless Steel Sheets\n---------------------------------------------------------------\nProduct Classification Type: HTS US\nPredicted Classification Code: 722090   Confidence: 95% ✔️  (Source : LLM)\nCustom Description: \"Flat-rolled stainless steel sheets, 2 mm thickness, used in manufacturing.\"\nStatus: Compliant ✔️\n\n---------------------------------------------------------------\nEXTRACTED TECHNICAL ATTRIBUTES\n---------------------------------------------------------------\n- Material: Stainless Steel\n- Thickness: 2 mm\n- Form: Flat-rolled sheets\n- Keywords Detected: \"industrial manufacturing,\" \"flat-rolled,\" \"stainless steel\"\n\n---------------------------------------------------------------\nCLASSIFICATION BREAKDOWN\n---------------------------------------------------------------\n- HS Code 7220.90 falls under Chapter 72: Iron and Steel\n- Detailed Breakdown for 7220.90:\n            72 – Chapter: Iron and Steel\n            20 – Heading: Flat-rolled products of stainless steel, of a width of less than 600 mm\n            .90 – Subheading: Other\n\nTypical Sub-classifications under 7220 may include:\n7220.20 – Not further worked than cold-rolled (cold-reduced)\n7220.90 – Other (any stainless steel sheets, not cold-rolled, or with other further processing not specified above)\n\n---------------------------------------------------------------\nTARIFF & DUTY INFORMATION\n---------------------------------------------------------------\nRegion          Rate        Notes\n------------------------------------\nUS HTS          5.2%        ✔️\nEU TARIC        4.8%        ✔️\nPreferential    N/A          NAFTA/USMCA not applicable\n\n\n---------------------------------------------------------------\nEXPORT CONTROL & RESTRICTIONS\n---------------------------------------------------------------\nEAR Classification: Not Controlled ✔️\nDual-Use Item: No ✔️\nCountry-Specific Restrictions: None ✔️\n\n\n---------------------------------------------------------------\nSAFETY & STANDARDS COMPLIANCE\n---------------------------------------------------------------\nRoHS (EU): Compliant ✔️\nREACH (EU): Compliant ✔️\nFDA (US): Not applicable ✔️\nCE Marking: Not required ✔️\n\n---------------------------------------------------------------\nOTHER CLASSIFICATION TYPE SUGGESTIONS (EXPORT)\n---------------------------------------------------------------\nHTS IN: 7220.90 (India)\nHTS CA: 7220.90 (Canada)\nECCN: EAR99 (US Export Control)\nTARIC (EU): 7220900000\nUNSPSC: 30101806\nISIC: 2410\n\n---------------------------------------------------------------\nSUGGESTED NEXT STEPS\n---------------------------------------------\n\n---------------------------\nFollow below instructions always -\nInstruction to follow:\n- The value against Product Classification Type should be replaced with {{$context.$variables.prodClassType}}\n- The value against Source should be replaced with {{$context.$variables.source}}\n- The value against Predicted Classification Code should be replaced with  {{$context.$variables.classificationCode}} .\n- The value against Confidence should be replaced with {{$context.$variables.predictionConfidence}}. \n- The value against Custom Description should be replaced with {{$context.$nodes.CUSTOMS_DESCRIPTION_GENERATOR.$output.customsDescription}} .\n- Under \"EXTRACTED TECHNICAL ATTRIBUTES\",  do not ever display the words  {{$context.$variables.domain}} or \"remarkQualifier\" or \"remarkText\". \n- DO NOT EVER add any section like or related to \"ADDITIONAL HELP I CAN PROVIDE\"\n- No listing of other tasks you can perform.\n- No follow-up prompts like “Would you like…” or \"If you want I can...\"\n- Under \"SUGGESTED NEXT STEPS\", based on the information you have, suggest a list of steps as bullet points that the user can do next to be compliant.\n- Strictly follow the above sample format. Use tabular and bullet points, avoid long paragraphs. For table to format, it has to be in html format inside a div tag. (div > table > tr > td )\n- Under \"OTHER CLASSIFICATION TYPE SUGGESTIONS\", Suggest 3 to 5 other potentially relevant classification types/codes fitting for the product and region, e.g., if US HTS is present, also list classification code fields for \"HTS IN\", \"HTS CA\", \"ECCN\", or any other regionally relevant system"
            }
          ],
          "type": "LLM"
        },
        {
