          "inputs": [
            {
              "id": "1767332845618_1",
              "name": "prompt",
              "type": "string",
              "value": "Display {{$context.$nodes.GET_MANUFACTURED_ITEM_COMPONENT_DETAILS.$output}} + {{$context.$nodes.PREDICT_CLASSIFICATION_CODE_FOR_M_ITEM.$output}} in below format -\n\nSample format\n----------------------------------------\nItem : SMARTPHONE\nPredicted Classification Code : ** **     Confidence: 95%\nProduct Classification Type : HTS US\n\n-----------------------------\nCOMPONENT\tQUANTITY \tTOTAL VALUE (USD)\tHTS US CODE\nLithium-Ion Battery\t1\t$10–$15\t8507600020\n....\n----------------------------------------------------\n\n\nInstructions to follow for formatting-\n- Render \"COMPONENTS\" section in tabular format. For table to format, it has to be in html format inside a div tag. (div > table > tr > td ).\n- Replace SMARTPHONE with {{$context.$nodes.EXTRACT_REQUIRED_FIELDS_FROM_ITEM.$output.itemName}} and {{$context.$nodes.EXTRACT_REQUIRED_FIELDS_FROM_ITEM.$output.brandName}} for \"Item\" .\n- Use {{$context.$nodes.PREDICT_CLASSIFICATION_CODE_FOR_M_ITEM.$output.predictedClassificationCode}} for \"Predicted Classification Code\".\n- Use {{$context.$nodes.PREDICT_CLASSIFICATION_CODE_FOR_M_ITEM.$output.confidence}} for \"Confidence\".\n- Use {{$context.$variables.prodClassType}} for \"Product Classification Type\".\n- Consider {{$context.$nodes.APPROVE_CLASSIFICATION_DETAILS_FOR_MANUFACTURED_ITEM.$feedbackRecieved}} for suggestions but do not alter any data from {{$context.$nodes.GET_MANUFACTURED_ITEM_COMPONENT_DETAILS.$output}} in the output.\n- Never display {{$context.$variables.domain}} or URL encoding to the user.\n- DO NOT add any \"Note\" or display to the user any instructions given."
            }
          ],
          "type": "LLM"
        },
